ing to be in a class later in the  future  that's not necessarily part of the same  consideration process  um so for many of you round three might  actually be a good idea  for college seniors that gives you more  time your senior year to do things  oftentimes this is a year when you might  have some leadership potential  or leadership roles or are doing some  internships  so this gives you more time to kind of  build up your experience set  and maybe have experiences you want to  talk about in that application  all right here's a question from rashmi  how has the global experiences program  been adapted in light of the pandemic  so great question here i think this has  been one of those spaces that we  continue to evolve  as we take best practices and as we  monitor the travel policies not just  of the university but also of the  different countries  that our folks might be going to so last  year  um we there's a program called the gmix  the graduate management immersion  experience  you can think about that almost as an  internship somewhere in the world  during the summer between your mba 1 and  mba 2 year  so last year many of them shifted to  virtual  and hopefully we're going to be able to  offer those again virtually this summer  not knowing what the exact travel  possibilities are going to look like  i know our global studies department is  working really really hard to  figure out different ways to incorporate  those global perspectives  into your education and so actually one  of those new programs this year is  global dialogues  which brings together students from all  different backgrounds speakers from all  over the world  to talk about what does it mean to both  create community  and engage with others regardless of  what cultural or geographic  setting you're in how do you step back  have some of the internal dialogue that  allows you to unpack  both you know the individual group and  environment factors  that might influence the way that you  need to carry yourself  to be effective so multiple ways there  more space for evolution and it's  definitely something that the school is  keeping an eye on because  that global experience and global  perspective  is a really important part of kind of  your development journey  all right um question here  um from puja earlier we heard so i  talked about different teaching methods  this year a lot of classes are online  where simulation and action leadership  classes affected  so yes and no so there has been an  evolution in some of the course  offerings some of them have been shifted  more online  as i mentioned earlier some of them are  meeting in small group sessions  outdoors we're lucky enough to be in  california where  the environment allows for us to have  outdoor classes all the way into the  fall and  into the winter really so some of those  courses are still being held  in very much the same format or very  similar formats to what they used to be  and actually very interesting silver  lining to  some of the classes being online because  of this  newfound like um fluency with zoom  it opens up a whole new world of who is  visiting as case protagonist who's  engaging with students  whether it is globally this is a whole  new range of diversity and perspectives  that has opened up to us so there have  also been some really interesting silver  linings to the experience along the way  all right so we're getting close to the  top of the hour  um right now i really want to encourage  you so we might not have gone to all the  questions in the q  a box but we have a whole week of  exploration  with diversity and leadership many more  sessions featuring  admissions staff so bring those  questions there if they're not already  answered  or if you don't find the answer by  exploring our website  you know this is another time to to come  talk to us and be  a part of um the experience  again registration for events is open  all week long so  maybe you're curious to hear a little  bit more about the experience for  active duty or military veterans or  you're thinking about  hey i'm curious about working in latin  america  check out the session featuring our  global some of our global interest clubs  including the latin american student  association texas club and the midwest  club  really thinking about that vertical time  zone slice some of the different  aspects that can really complement your  experience here at the gsb  so with that thank you so much for  joining us for the kickoff  i hope to see you throughout this week  and  regardless if you're starting the day or  ending your day  thank you again for joining us stay safe  stay hydrated find moments of support  solidarity and gratitude you too can go  out there  change lives change organizations and  change the world we'll see you soon

